    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῠδοιμ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make an uproar, spread confusion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼ δ᾽ ἀν᾽ ὅμιλον ἰόντε κυδοίμεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.324
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				13.480
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>drive in confusion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέας εἶσι κυδοιμήσων ἐς Ὄλυμπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.136
				</span></i>
			. (In later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Piet.</u>
				145
			</span></i>.)</div>
